IMPORT prelude
-- Running a rule that uses EVERY. The companion to every-example.l4, which
-- shows the shapes; this one shows the shapes working.
--
-- Every rule here names its group with `WHO elem t tenants` — the roll. That
-- is what makes it runnable: see "Where the group comes from" on EVERY.md.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Pay     HAS payer  IS AN Actor, payee IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER
    Receipt HAS issuer IS AN Actor, to    IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
carol       MEANS Tenant OF "Carol"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob, carol

-- THE BARRIER. Every tenant signs; when the last of them has, the landlord
-- owes a delivery, and his five days run from that moment.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        WHO    elem t tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5)
        LEST   BREACH

-- Alice on day 1, Bob on day 2, Carol on day 9: the group is complete on day
-- 9, so the delivery is due on day 14, and a delivery on day 13 is in time.
#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 2
  PARTY carol DOES Sign carol AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 13

-- Carol never signs, so the group's obligation fails and the LEST fires.
#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 2
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 20

-- THE FORK. Each tenant who pays earns a receipt of their own, within five
-- days of their own payment.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`receipts` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        WHO    elem t tenants
        MUST   Pay (EXACTLY t) (EXACTLY theLandlord) amount
        WITHIN 7
        UPON   EACH
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord
                    MUST   Receipt (EXACTLY theLandlord) (EXACTLY t) (EXACTLY amount)
                    WITHIN 5)
        LEST   BREACH BY t

#TRACE `receipts` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 1
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord alice 100 AT 2
  PARTY bob   DOES Pay bob   theLandlord 200 AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord bob 200 AT 4
  PARTY carol DOES Pay carol theLandlord 300 AT 5
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord carol 300 AT 6

-- Bob does not pay: his branch fails, and the breach names him.
#TRACE `receipts` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 1
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord alice 100 AT 2
  PARTY carol DOES Pay carol theLandlord 300 AT 5
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord carol 300 AT 6
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord bob 200 AT 20
